<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tokugawa Iemitsu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1604–1651</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tokugawa Iemitsu was the third Tokugawa <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, ruling from 1623 to 1651. He completed the shogunate's system of control, making alternate attendance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> in Edo compulsory, suppressing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimabara-rebellion">Shimabara Rebellion</a> of 1637–38 and restricting foreign trade to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and Chinese at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki">Nagasaki</a>. In 1643 he gave the domain of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aizu">Aizu</a> to his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoshina-masayuki">Hoshina Masayuki</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tokugawa-iemitsu.jpg" alt="Tokugawa Iemitsu" width="320" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The author creates a file. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iemitu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
